From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:04:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Give the braille gesture hint a theme that defines its
 colours

The braille keyboard's change gesture screen colours the title of each
hint with the Material 3 roles colorTertiaryFixed (a hint) and
colorErrorContainer (a warning), read through
MaterialColors.getColor(context, attr, message) from a context wrapped in
the CustomGestureView style. That style inherited
Theme.MaterialComponents.Light, which defines neither role, so the call
threw IllegalArgumentException and TalkBack crashed each time the
"Continue" button of the "How to change a gesture" dialog opened the
screen.

Of the stock themes only the Material 3 family defines the two roles. The
style now inherits Theme.Material3.Light, so the lookup resolves to
Material's own palette: pale roles that read the same in light and dark
mode, because the style is a light theme whatever the system setting and
the hint is drawn on a fixed dark scrim. Nothing else reads the style.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 braille/brailleime/src/phone/res/values/styles.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/braille/brailleime/src/phone/res/values/styles.xml b/braille/brailleime/src/phone/res/values/styles.xml
index b70d8d130b39b0f43518e9ebbeec4da85dcff4bf..e201044c466846821b12b47f56fce583fa372604 100644
--- a/braille/brailleime/src/phone/res/values/styles.xml
+++ b/braille/brailleime/src/phone/res/values/styles.xml
@@ -75,5 +75,5 @@
 
   <style name="KeyboardDialogStyle" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight" />
 
-  <style name="CustomGestureView" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents.Light" />
+  <style name="CustomGestureView" parent="@style/Theme.Material3.Light" />
 </resources>
\ No newline at end of file
